  "prompt": "From SCOUT's Quad Cities flood dataset in the Data Catalog, load three of its files by name: the nature-based solution classes, NBS_others_5m.tif, and the flood depth with and without nature-based solutions for a projection period the user picks from 2020 - 2040, 2050 - 2080 and 2080 - 2100, 2020 - 2040 by default, all read over a bounding box of west, south, east and north the user can change, by default the west of the area so it fits a map. Then run SCOUT's flood simulation twice on them as two scenarios: one with every nature-based solution in place and one with none. Draw each scenario's flood depth on its own Autark map in blues, and compute each one's median and mean depth with Raster Statistics. Finally, map the difference between the two scenarios, with nature-based solutions minus without, and chart their median flood depths side by side. The flood simulation is not part of the standard node set, so whatever provides it needs installing first.",
